     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<div style=\"margin:6px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:0.85em; margin-bottom:4px;\"><b>Deuterium retention in W after DIII-D exposure (ERDA, areal)</b></div><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"max-width:600px; width:auto; height:auto; display:block;\"/></div>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.HTML object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "The 800 K He pre-exposure is the only case that reduces D retention, and only in H-mode. The 600 K He pre-exposure increases retention in both modes. The two He pre-exposure temperatures differ in more than temperature — the 600 K exposure ran 9× longer at 7× lower flux — so the temperature and flux/duration effects are confounded.\n",
       "\n",
       "**NRA (depth-resolved)** confirms the ERDA pattern and adds depth information:\n",
       "\n",
       "| Sample | Surface (0–0.5 µm) | Sub-surface (0.5–3 µm) | Total | Ratio |\n",
       "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
       "| W-DH | 1.80×10¹⁵ | 2.98×10¹⁴ | 2.10×10¹⁵ | 1.00 |\n",
       "| W-He600-DH | 2.06×10¹⁵ | 3.95×10¹⁴ | 2.46×10¹⁵ | 1.17 |\n",
       "| W-He800-DH | 5.82×10¹⁴ | 6.96×10¹³ | 6.52×10¹⁴ | 0.31 |\n",
       "| W-DL | 2.00×10¹⁵ | 6.57×10¹⁴ | 2.66×10¹⁵ | 1.00 |\n",
       "| W-He600-DL | 4.42×10¹⁵ | 4.97×10¹⁴ | 4.92×10¹⁵ | 1.85 |\n",
       "| W-He800-DL | 2.69×10¹⁵ | 2.70×10¹⁴ | 2.96×10¹⁵ | 1.11 |"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
